      "id": "source-2",
      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T18:49:30Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and 634-frame call trace, pool creation transaction and trace, verified Vyper 0.3.0 source, historical runtime at deployment and immediately before the exploit, commit-pinned reproduction, Vyper's compiler advisory, LlamaRisk's pool-by-pool post-mortem, exact post-transaction token balances, and the later whitehat exploit and return receipts. The malicious anchor repeatedly executes the direct CRV/ETH pool 0x8301ae4fc9c624d1d396cbdaa1ed877821d7c511 without DELEGATECALL. The pool was created by top-level CREATE from 0xbabe61887f1de2713c6f97e567623453d3c79f67 in transaction 0x5fccb9a4416f29918bf376294a8121834173a4a4499bcb1f98a336cac54cfa6e. Its 22,389-byte runtime is byte-identical at deployment and block 17807829 and hashes to 0x0a93dc0d31254f712e0129e5a67ac2863dbf2c8505cf6f014b388792f75aadc1. After the flash loan is repaid, the attack helper's balances increase by exactly 7,680.493699345042585217 WETH and 7,193,401.775311984312323106 CRV. Independent actors attacked the pETH/ETH, msETH/ETH, and alETH/ETH pools; those losses are not part of this incident."
